    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all 3 tests green (lowercase-on-store, reject-invalid, accept-missing).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented optional owner `email`: syntactically validated, stored and returned lower-cased, rejected with 400 when present but invalid.\n\nThe change follows the codebase's existing `NormalizeTelephone` pattern \u2014 a small, single-method step wired into the POST pipeline \u2014 rather than growing any existing class:\n\n- **`NormalizeEmail.java`** (new) \u2014 the whole behaviour lives here in one 8-line method with zero surrounding complexity: skip if absent, reject malformed via the existing `MissingFieldsException` (\u2192400), otherwise lower-case and store back on the request DTO. Reusing `MissingFieldsException` is consistent with how `NormalizeTelephone` already rejects a present-but-malformed telephone.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted one `normalizeEmail` step between telephone normalization and the build step.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` (`format: email`) property to the `OwnerFields` schema, which regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with the accessors; MapStruct maps it by name, so no mapper edit.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `email` column field plus a trivial getter/setter for persistence and mapping.\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added an `email` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql), and updated the hsqldb seed `data.sql` (the only one using positional inserts) so its rows stay column-aligned.\n\nNo existing method's complexity grew; the new logic is isolated in its own cohesive unit.",
